        "tipo": "gramatica",
        "min": 10,
        "titulo": "Verb in second position, questions and negatives",
        "explicacao": "The conjugated verb always sits in 2nd position. If the sentence starts with something else (today, tomorrow), the subject moves to after the verb: «Heute arbeite ich.» In yes/no questions, the verb comes 1st — no \"do\" needed: «Wohnst du in Berlin?» (Do you live in Berlin?). In questions with a question word, the word comes 1st and the verb 2nd: «Wo wohnst du?» The negative «nicht» goes after the verb («Ich arbeite nicht» = I don't work) or before what it negates («Ich wohne nicht in Berlin»). To say you like doing something, put «gern» after the verb: «Ich lerne gern Deutsch» (I like learning German).",
